The Riders shall not be combatted in melee and can perfectly taken out at
the door using a wand of death (in the two cases I need to face) or a bunch
of enchanted daggers, depending on the class played. At the Sanctum it's
different; mostly I have no straight line to target the priest from afar,
and one has to actively enter the Sanctum while the priest approaches.
I've had as well other games, where I could wait until the High Priest and
a double troubled Wizard where all in a straight line as seen through the
open door. Games vary. Equipment varies. Situations vary or are different.
There's no such thing as a well defined "ascension-ready"-ness.

Differences like those makes a plain comparison of damage just a non-starter.

But I admit that your games may be differing from mine and your requirements
might make sense for how you play.

